 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124500 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186124847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186290485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186124230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124501 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186125372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1045 "The Parametric Equations of a Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186125368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124717 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ca8227e6-ef47-5702-8c4f-321ab31e8355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t-12 \\\\ y=-5-7t \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{4}t+\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6ab6a329-d125-54e3-98aa-c411b7b2d383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124779 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-12 \\\\ -5-7t \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}t+\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -7t \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-12,-5,\\frac{1}{5})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1071 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $4-t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9a10a92-511c-5609-8370-301fff1b284f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124846 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-3t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36023" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5 \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9efb0092-3045-58e2-bed4-ca88fc8fe6c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186124949 #edb/ref 1074 "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125368 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125368 #edb/ref 1061 189149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125368 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de4015ef-1002-54f7-adee-e5eee4e87979" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125368 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125369 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125369 #edb/ref 1061 189150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125369 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c0d5ba6-1e60-5d4d-b42e-60ba32609db6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125369 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125370 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125370 #edb/ref 1061 189153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125370 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5810a9c-9d11-54cc-9534-f5807fd71ff5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125370 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125371 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186125372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125371 #edb/ref 1061 189156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125371 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "83088d79-842b-5477-8d05-56eb6c96e451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125371 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125372 #edb/ref 1061 189159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5a457aae-70d6-5725-8620-6593b8838a70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186124501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125899 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we have a straight line passing through the point $P(3,-1,7)$ and that's parallel to the direction vector ![](images/54/54405c5c6e2502e5174525c2ee36a99366a79933b47e316a09858f827fda8dae.svg) As we know, we can write the vector equation of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nUsing the vector equation above, we can create a set of **parametric equations** where we express a general point $(x,y,z)$ in terms of  the parameter $t.$\n\nIf we let ![](images/67/67b8360f90540ffb75d39717c375f0ef6e9a8a39cae5832c78957105e0d148b6.svg) be the position vector of the general point $(x,y,z),$ then the above equation can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1+5t \\\\ 7-3t\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n![](images/64/64cf325014eff341673557321ef565e35988b836630f3fbeb52af8024d7aaad7.svg)\n\nThe equations in the above system are called the **parametric equations** of the straight line.\nGeometrically, the equation states that a point belongs to the line if and only if its coordinates have the form\n\n$$\n(3, \\: -1+5t, \\: 7-3t),\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\n![](images/e2/e29ce95cdccb47b97578f6431a96e608f7af9f6709410b221ff517b436896608.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125899 #edb/ref 1065 9660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125899 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6ff73cc8-91a0-5a25-9c14-6e87496adac8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186125899 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259941 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11-2t \\\\ z=4+7t\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259941 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259941 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06f568ab-a709-5bca-88dc-51b139dea190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260110 #edb/ref 1080 "r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260110 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260110 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b3ac191-12b6-5c33-91e8-bbd4a678d9f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260284 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2d9646e2-26ba-